From 430549af183137bc901f894037b8692feb697dca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] config: enable save-exact in .npmrc to pin new dependencies

When a developer runs 'npm install pkg' or 'bun add pkg', the default
behavior saves a semver range (^x.y.z) in package.json. This opens the
door to silent minor/patch upgrades that can introduce supply-chain
risk or behavioral drift between installs.

save-exact=true pins new deps to the exact installed version
("pkg": "1.2.3"), making every install reproducible and forcing
version bumps to be intentional. Both npm and bun respect this setting.
---
 .npmrc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/.npmrc b/.npmrc
index b6f27f1..d9ca886 100644
--- a/.npmrc
+++ b/.npmrc
@@ -1 +1,2 @@
 engine-strict=true
+save-exact=true
-- 
